🌐 Web Application Basics

Jab tum browser me koi website open karte ho, basic process:

Browser → Request → Web Server → Response → Browser

Example:

Chrome → tryhackme.com → Server → HTML/CSS/JS → Chrome

Website ke 2 main parts hote hain:

1. Frontend / Client-Side

Jo cheez user ke browser me run/display hoti hai.

Main technologies:

HTML → structure
CSS → design/style
JavaScript → interaction/functionality
2. Backend / Server-Side

Server par run hone wala part.

Ye:

requests process karta hai
database se data leta hai
authentication handle karta hai
response browser ko bhejta hai
🏗️ HTML

HTML = HyperText Markup Language

HTML website ka skeleton/structure hai.

Example:

<html>
<head>
    <title>My Website</title>
</head>

<body>
    <h1>Hello</h1>
    <p>Welcome!</p>
</body>
</html>

Important tags
Tag	Meaning
<html>	Complete HTML document
<head>	Page ki information
<title>	Browser tab ka title
<body>	Visible content
<h1>	Large heading
<p>	Paragraph
<button>	Button
<img>	Image
Attributes

Tags ke andar extra information dene ke liye attributes use hote hain.

<p class="red">Hello</p>


Yahan:

class = attribute
"red" = value
id vs class
<p id="user1">Alice</p>
<p class="users">Bob</p>
<p class="users">Jim</p>


id normally unique hoti hai.

class multiple elements par use ho sakti hai.

🟨 JavaScript

HTML = structure

CSS = looks

JavaScript = behaviour

Example:

document.getElementById("demo").innerHTML = "Hack the Planet";


Ye demo ID wale element ka text change kar dega.

JavaScript user interaction bhi handle kar sakti hai:

<button onclick="alert('Hello')">Click Me</button>


Button click karne par JavaScript execute hogi.

🔓 Sensitive Data Exposure

Ye cybersecurity ke liye bahut important hai.

Kabhi-kabhi developer galti se sensitive information frontend source code me chhod deta hai.

Example:

<!-- Temporary password: admin123 -->


Ya:

username = "admin";
password = "secret123";


Ya hidden page:

<a href="/admin-panel">Admin</a>


Browser ko jo HTML/JS milta hai, user uska source dekh sakta hai.

Isliye:

Website assess karte waqt:

Right Click → View Page Source

check karna useful hai.

⚠️ Important: "hidden" HTML ka matlab secure nahi hota. Agar browser ko data bheja gaya hai, user potentially usse inspect kar sakta hai.

💉 HTML Injection

Ab actual vulnerability.

Simple definition:

HTML Injection tab hota hai jab user ka input properly filter/sanitize nahi kiya jata aur directly webpage me HTML ke form me render ho jata hai.

Suppose website me form hai:

What's your name?
[ Alice             ]


Website output karti hai:

Hello Alice


Normal hai.

Lekin attacker input kare:

<h1>Hello</h1>


Agar website input ko sanitize nahi karti, browser ise text ki tarah nahi, HTML ki tarah interpret kar sakta hai.

Result:

Hello

Matlab attacker webpage ka appearance/control manipulate kar sakta hai.

🧼 Input Sanitisation

Sanitisation = user ke input ko clean/filter karna before using it.

Example:

User input:

<h1>Hello</h1>


Application usse safe text me convert kare:

<h1>Hello</h1>


Instead of actually rendering it as a heading.

Golden Rule 🔥

Never trust user input.

User jo bhi input de raha hai, usse automatically trustworthy nahi maan sakte.

🧠 HTML Injection vs JavaScript

HTML Injection ka impact sirf HTML tak limited nahi ho sakta.

Agar application dangerous user-controlled content ko page me inject hone de, JavaScript execution bhi possible ho sakti hai, depending on how the application handles the input.

Isliye:

Unsanitised input → HTML injection → potentially script injection/XSS

Lekin terminology yaad rakho:

HTML Injection → HTML inject karna
XSS (Cross-Site Scripting) → browser me attacker-controlled JavaScript execute karwana
